<title>CANADA: Canada Dec wage settlements average 0.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada Dec wage settlements average 0.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Annual wage increases in Canadian collective bargaining agreements reached in December averaged 0.7 percent, down from 1.9 percent in November, the Department of Human Resources Development said on Thursday.</p>
<p>			   Agreements/employees    Pct change</p>
<p>Public sector	 13/32,876		     +0.4</p>
<p>Private sector	10/43,237		     +1.0</p>
<p>Wage increases are the average annual percentage increase in base rates -- the wage rate of the lowest paid classification in a bargaining unit -- over the term of the agreement in settlements negotiated during the period shown.</p>
<p>Statistics Canada said annual wage settlements averaged 0.9 percent for the whole year 1996, unchanged from 1995.</p>
<p>(For more information on the settlements, contact Human Resources Development's Workplace Information Directorate, at 1-800-567-6866 or 819-997-3117.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
